================================================================================
Node.js
================================================================================

oam vendors Node.js in two separate places, both under the MIT license.
Copyright Node.js contributors; portions copyright Joyent, Inc. and other Node
contributors (per-file headers retained in the vendored sources). Like V8's,
this notice is hand-maintained: neither tree is a cargo dependency, so neither
can be collected by `cargo about`.

  1. js/vendor/node-streams/ -- SHIPPED IN THE BINARY. lib/stream.js,
     lib/stream/promises.js and lib/internal/streams/*, compiled into the
     startup snapshot. The upstream tag, per-file checksums and refresh
     procedure live in js/vendor/node-streams/UPSTREAM.

  2. conformance/vendor/node/ -- REPOSITORY ONLY, not in the binary. A pinned
     v22.22.2 snapshot of a subset of nodejs/node (lib/, deps/, test/), used by
     the node-suite conformance harness. Node's own LICENSE ships alongside it
     at conformance/vendor/node/LICENSE; provenance is in the README there.

The full MIT text is reproduced in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md ("Node.js" section)
and at conformance/vendor/node/LICENSE.

